{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":": counts pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overflows only past "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range, to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"type":"text","text":". When every weight is an integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees(weight:)-28jjs"]}],"metadata":{"title":"numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE21numberOfSpanningTrees6weightSdqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_tSBRd__lF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/ElectricalNetworks.swift#L64"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex. NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"number_of_spanning_trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)-28jjs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","preci